WEBVTT

00:00.750 --> 00:04.750
I was told to become your father only a moment ago.

00:05.160 --> 00:11.740
But, since I am involved in the mission, I will do my best to be your father and not shame anyone with what I do.

00:10.920 --> 00:11.740
It's what I was meant to be.

00:11.740 --> 00:13.490
What? The game?

00:13.490 --> 00:16.110
That doesn't count.

00:16.110 --> 00:18.370
Let me ask just in case. Why?

00:18.370 --> 00:21.460
Because I am the one and only absolute being in this world.

00:21.460 --> 00:24.190
In this family, I am the rule!

00:22.910 --> 00:27.500
How should I describe this atrocious condition I'm in?

00:28.410 --> 00:30.050
Family Frenzy.

01:50.130 --> 01:51.380
Have you gone to the bathroom already?

01:51.430 --> 01:52.650
How about your prayers to this Kyouka-sama?

01:52.650 --> 01:54.840
Are you ready to sit in the corner of the room and stare at your TV?

02:15.560 --> 02:18.240
It looked really good, didn't it?

02:16.530 --> 02:18.240
What a bother...

02:18.240 --> 02:20.750
But I don't think I would have been able to eat all that.

02:18.910 --> 02:22.720
Having a large family means having
a lot of loads of laundry to do, I guess.

02:21.190 --> 02:22.860
Next, here's your weather forecast for today.

02:22.860 --> 02:27.050
The sun is out right now in the metro area, but clouds should start covering up the sky starting in the afternoon.

02:22.860 --> 02:24.240
Ah, I'm so sleepy.

02:24.240 --> 02:26.180
Coming home in the morning makes everything so tiring.

02:26.250 --> 02:27.660
Welcome home, Ginichi-san.

02:27.050 --> 02:30.680
The wind will pick up, and depending on the area, we may see some showers.

02:28.070 --> 02:29.870
Thank you for taking care of the laundry.

02:29.870 --> 02:31.300
I'll take it upstairs if you like.

02:30.680 --> 02:35.220
To anyone doing their laundry right now, I suggest hanging them indoors today.

02:32.300 --> 02:34.590
It's fine. I can handle this.

02:35.780 --> 02:36.780
Chika-chan.

02:36.780 --> 02:37.590
Y-Yes?

02:38.850 --> 02:41.260
Ginichi-san is acting so manly all of a sudden.

02:42.290 --> 02:44.360
Chika-chan! Your skin looks so smooth this morning!

02:44.360 --> 02:46.410
What cosmetics do you use?
Is it face lotion? Is it emulsion cream?

02:46.410 --> 02:47.390
Or is it because you're young?

02:47.390 --> 02:49.210
Oh no, I can't just stand here!

02:49.210 --> 02:50.020
I better get my sleep!

02:50.020 --> 02:52.460
Sleep deprivation is bad for your skin!

02:53.680 --> 02:54.440
That's it?

02:54.440 --> 02:56.940
Here are more celebrity news.

02:56.940 --> 02:58.570
Next up:

02:57.600 --> 03:00.450
I've got to find a way to get Ginichi-san back to being manly.

02:58.570 --> 03:00.450
Revelation of Passionate Love.

03:00.450 --> 03:02.570
The birth of a couple that ignores time.

03:02.570 --> 03:07.400
We've learned about a relationship between Tamino-san, a member of the Jacklack, and Yano-san, an actress.

03:07.400 --> 03:10.960
They were scooped while they were on Hawaii for prenuptial traveling.

03:10.960 --> 03:12.460
No pictures, please.

03:12.460 --> 03:13.960
Their meeting was not a drama, but...

03:14.540 --> 03:15.470
This is it!

03:25.490 --> 03:28.600
I heard August 2nd is traditionally the day for honeymoons!

03:28.600 --> 03:32.680
If you're looking for a honeymoon plan, please look through the large selection in our catalogue.

03:29.580 --> 03:31.350
You're as random as ever.

03:31.350 --> 03:35.750
How dare you keep something like this a secret from the wife you swore to be together with for the rest of your life?

03:34.800 --> 03:36.180
Good morning, Kyouka.

03:36.180 --> 03:38.820
That's right. I'm the wife, and I'm telling you to put hijacking in the itinerary, too.

03:38.820 --> 03:43.930
Hijacking? That's not included in any of our packages, but we can prepare a luxurious flight.

03:39.230 --> 03:42.780
Really, if Chika hadn't told me about it,
we would have missed the date.

03:42.780 --> 03:43.830
Chika-san?

03:43.930 --> 03:46.200
No! I want to go to Mu!

03:46.960 --> 03:47.830
She hung up on me.

03:47.830 --> 03:50.330
Kitty, here's the next place.

03:48.910 --> 03:50.330
All right, I'll settle it with the next place.

03:50.330 --> 03:56.000
Comfy~ Comfy~ Comfy~

03:50.330 --> 03:53.570
The next place will be the 264th try.

03:54.480 --> 03:56.000
Why not give up already?

03:56.000 --> 03:58.980
How could I give up on such a big event so easily?!

03:58.980 --> 04:01.600
That's right! Ginichi-san's and my future depends on this.

04:00.750 --> 04:01.600
That's right!

04:02.000 --> 04:05.060
Honored Brother and Honored Sister
are newly wed, as well?

04:05.060 --> 04:07.300
They're not, so she's panicking.

04:07.300 --> 04:09.400
Are we taking the children, too?

04:09.400 --> 04:13.920
Though now that I say it, going alone with you makes me feel endangered.

04:13.920 --> 04:16.810
What a nonsensical question to ask of Kyouka-sama.

04:17.230 --> 04:18.900
Of course we're all going together!

04:18.900 --> 04:20.330
Yay!

04:20.330 --> 04:21.320
Hello?

04:22.650 --> 04:24.830
I sense danger.

04:26.490 --> 04:28.020
Hey, is this a travel agency?

04:28.020 --> 04:31.580
The omnipotent god, Kyouka-sama, is giving a call, so listen well.

04:31.580 --> 04:34.190
The world turns with smiles.

04:34.190 --> 04:36.290
Trust comes first. Customers come first.

04:36.290 --> 04:41.050
Sakurai Travel Agency, Tokyo Office,
Branch No. 3, Sakurai Chieri speaking.

04:41.050 --> 04:43.720
You're calling for a honeymoon plan?

04:44.430 --> 04:47.540
The Midarezaki family, composed of
five people, two animals, and one robot.

04:48.090 --> 04:51.400
Five people, two animals, and one robot, was that correct?

04:51.400 --> 04:53.060
Will this be a family trip?

04:53.060 --> 04:55.840
A honeymoon composed of five people, two animals, and one robot, I said.

04:56.240 --> 04:57.710
Do you have a place in mind?

04:57.710 --> 04:59.940
The Mu! Where else?!

05:01.440 --> 05:04.530
While it is a standard, Hawaii remains very popular.

05:05.740 --> 05:08.490
Oh, and put a hijack event on as an option, please.

05:08.490 --> 05:10.580
We go by safety first.

05:10.580 --> 05:11.990
Please don't worry about any hijacks.

05:11.990 --> 05:14.690
You intend to go against me no matter what, don't you?

05:14.690 --> 05:16.210
Only because we care about you.

05:16.210 --> 05:17.830
Don't take me lightly!

05:17.830 --> 05:20.840
Since you're over the phone, I couldn't measure your weight even if I wanted to.

05:20.840 --> 05:22.320
What did you say?!

05:22.320 --> 05:23.960
Looks like the operator is putting up a good fight.

05:23.960 --> 05:28.490
From what I've heard so far, it sounds
as though you don't have a clear vision yet.

05:28.490 --> 05:32.430
If you would come over to the office,
we could give suggestions over some pamphlets.

05:32.840 --> 05:35.560
You're telling me to come over?!

05:33.250 --> 05:35.980
This is the 264th call!

05:39.790 --> 05:43.480
Fine. My child is begging me, so I'll go over to your place.

05:43.920 --> 05:46.690
Then we'll be expecting you tomorrow.

05:48.300 --> 05:50.350
As expected from the deputy branch chief.

05:50.350 --> 05:53.890
If we can get the customer to come, the deal is pretty much set.

05:53.890 --> 05:55.670
Leave the preparations to us.

05:55.670 --> 05:58.710
We're sure to make the top sales this month, too.

05:59.010 --> 06:01.540
We don't care about sales.

06:01.540 --> 06:05.770
What's important is having the heart to provide our customers with a comfortable trip.

06:06.160 --> 06:08.550
Let's be ready tomorrow.

06:08.550 --> 06:11.680
Always with a smile, and customers always come first.

06:11.680 --> 06:13.980
Yeah!

06:13.980 --> 06:15.290
Yeah!

06:14.740 --> 06:16.230
We're so blessed.

06:16.230 --> 06:18.700
Make sure to always smile, everyone.

06:18.700 --> 06:20.400
Sparkle!

06:18.700 --> 06:20.400
Yeah!

06:24.070 --> 06:27.340
That Sakurai Chieri is so sassy.

06:27.780 --> 06:31.740
To take all the underling's attention, leaving me, the branch head, aside.

06:36.830 --> 06:38.490
Unforgivable.

06:38.490 --> 06:40.830
Tomorrow's customer will be mine.

06:45.550 --> 06:47.940
Please! Eat me!

06:47.940 --> 06:50.720
Is this rat poison or something?

06:50.720 --> 06:52.450
How rude of you.

06:52.450 --> 06:56.860
You would have been crucified on any other day, but lucky for you, I'm in a good mood today.

06:56.860 --> 06:58.100
Now, listen well.

06:58.100 --> 07:07.610
The three fastest to finish this wonderful dish created by none other than myself get to go to the travel agency with me.

07:00.600 --> 07:03.610
Danger. Danger. This is poison, Mother.

07:03.610 --> 07:05.390
You can do it, Ginichi-san.

07:05.390 --> 07:07.080
Our future depends on this.

07:07.080 --> 07:08.070
Stop...

07:08.070 --> 07:11.290
No! Ginichi-san! Don't die!

07:14.620 --> 07:18.430
Father. Mother. Everyone else on the Earth. I'm sorry.

07:18.850 --> 07:23.360
Protecting the world may be too grave a task for me.

07:23.360 --> 07:23.920
I'm in.

07:24.910 --> 07:26.730
What do you mean, forfeiting?!

07:26.730 --> 07:29.800
Where did Suzuki-san go in middle of the preparation?

07:29.800 --> 07:32.280
Even Saitou-san's gone.

07:32.280 --> 07:33.640
Saitou-san!

07:34.760 --> 07:37.690
Ah, Andou-san. Have you seen Suzuki-san around?

07:37.690 --> 07:40.560
I saw Suzuki-san going towards the storage area.

07:40.560 --> 07:42.950
Even Saitou-san's missing.

07:42.950 --> 07:44.280
What should I do...

07:44.280 --> 07:46.520
Even the branch chief isn't around.

07:46.910 --> 07:48.530
How about I go take a quick look?

07:48.530 --> 07:52.630
Yeah, please. Midarezaki-sama should be coming soon, so make it quick.

07:52.630 --> 07:55.080
Please hold on!

07:55.080 --> 07:56.160
What is that?!

07:56.160 --> 07:57.120
Cat ears?

07:56.160 --> 07:57.120
Nyan!

07:58.580 --> 08:02.000
Everyone! Let's have some fun first, shall we?

08:04.080 --> 08:08.510
Deskworms won't be able to correctly greet this Kyouka-sama!

08:10.760 --> 08:12.520
Please stop!

08:12.880 --> 08:15.050
Ginichi-san, how does this look?

08:15.050 --> 08:16.640
Or, is this more romantic?

08:17.090 --> 08:19.110
Where did you come from, little girl?

08:19.110 --> 08:20.180
Would you like some candy?

08:20.180 --> 08:21.560
Kyouka-sama's coming through!

08:26.730 --> 08:29.510
Would you be Midarezaki-sama?

08:31.150 --> 08:32.680
Welcome.

08:32.680 --> 08:35.470
Andou-san, please prepare some tea for our guests.

08:35.470 --> 08:36.320
Right away.

08:38.580 --> 08:40.960
I've been expecting you, Kyouka-sama.

08:40.960 --> 08:43.800
I'm Sakurai Chieri, your representative.

08:44.510 --> 08:46.050
Kitty would be over there.

08:46.670 --> 08:49.000
Isn't she one of the "two animals"?

08:49.000 --> 08:50.130
No!

08:55.800 --> 08:58.640
I've prepared several itineraries today.

08:58.640 --> 09:02.630
Okay. Present me with any trash, and I'll shred you to pieces.

08:58.640 --> 09:02.430
Sign: In Use

09:02.630 --> 09:05.220
I hope you'll like them.

09:05.220 --> 09:07.370
We'll talk in the reception room.

09:06.150 --> 09:09.320
Sign: In Use

09:08.240 --> 09:09.690
This way please.

09:09.320 --> 09:12.280
Sign: In Use

09:10.000 --> 09:10.790
Huh?

09:10.790 --> 09:11.150
Huh?

09:12.280 --> 09:14.030
Sign: In Use

09:12.580 --> 09:13.160
Huh?

09:14.030 --> 09:15.400
Sign: In Use

09:14.110 --> 09:14.650
Huh?

09:15.280 --> 09:16.160
Huh?

09:15.400 --> 09:18.030
Sign: In Use

09:16.520 --> 09:18.030
Why?!

09:18.030 --> 09:20.880
How far do you plan on taking me?!

09:20.880 --> 09:23.560
My legs simply hurt, Mom.

09:23.560 --> 09:25.700
You're taking too much time.

09:25.700 --> 09:27.460
I'll start a ruckus if you don't end this soon.

09:27.460 --> 09:29.610
I-I'm very sorry.

09:29.610 --> 09:30.940
This way please.

09:33.020 --> 09:35.270
What are you doing? Let me through already.

09:40.140 --> 09:44.190
I-I'm sorry. This is some kind of mistake.

09:44.190 --> 09:45.810
What are you doing, Chief?

09:46.610 --> 09:47.500
Interesting!

09:48.530 --> 09:52.750
It's a little below par to be a welcome event for me, but for a beginner, it's not bad.

09:52.750 --> 09:54.390
It's simply mysterious.

09:54.390 --> 09:57.130
If it's a naked body, Ginichi-san has a better one.

09:57.130 --> 09:58.410
What? What?

09:59.010 --> 10:01.500
M-Midarezaki-sama, correct?

10:01.500 --> 10:05.230
I've heard the situation. I'm the branch chief, Doinki.

10:05.230 --> 10:06.390
On bara on bara.

10:06.390 --> 10:07.760
Please relax.

10:07.760 --> 10:10.850
What are you doing, Sakurai-kun? Bring them some tea.

10:10.850 --> 10:12.150
Andou-san is already getting the tea-

10:12.150 --> 10:13.540
Get a move on!

10:18.050 --> 10:20.460
I'm happy that the weather kept up for you.

10:20.460 --> 10:22.180
On bara on bara.

10:22.180 --> 10:24.540
And your children look very well, too.

10:24.540 --> 10:26.320
You're a restless guy, aren't you?

10:26.320 --> 10:28.620
I'm in a good mood, so don't worry.

10:28.620 --> 10:30.700
Tribal chief, go ahead and dance.

10:33.550 --> 10:34.260
Chika-chan.

10:34.260 --> 10:35.570
You see...

10:35.940 --> 10:40.820
Where did Andou-san go off to, making our customers wait?

10:42.540 --> 10:43.450
Are you all right?

10:43.830 --> 10:45.340
Thank you very much.

10:45.640 --> 10:46.810
Midarezaki-sama.

10:46.810 --> 10:48.170
What a horrible guy.

10:48.170 --> 10:50.130
We were worried, since you were taking so much time.

10:50.130 --> 10:51.190
So, go on.

10:51.910 --> 10:52.670
Yes.

10:52.670 --> 10:54.250
Thank you very much.

10:55.380 --> 10:56.870
Excuse me.

10:56.870 --> 10:58.940
What took you, Sakurai-san?

10:58.940 --> 11:01.640
Go to the storage room and get me the file on the Himalayas.

11:01.640 --> 11:03.410
The Himalayas?

11:03.740 --> 11:06.260
Um, Midarezaki-sama is here for a honeymoon trip-

11:05.170 --> 11:06.850
Get a move on!

11:06.950 --> 11:09.050
You mustn't make the customer wait.

11:11.740 --> 11:13.310
Let's see... This and...

11:14.860 --> 11:15.940
Woah there.

11:16.720 --> 11:19.420
Th-Thank you very much again.

11:19.420 --> 11:20.000
Here.

11:20.780 --> 11:22.180
Thank you very much.

11:22.180 --> 11:23.660
Right, go on now.

11:28.380 --> 11:29.850
Sorry to make you wait.

11:29.850 --> 11:32.620
You're slow! Bring us another helping of tea.

11:32.620 --> 11:36.630
That's enough. Let Chieri explain the trip.

11:36.630 --> 11:37.860
No, not yet!

11:37.860 --> 11:39.760
What are you doing, bring the tea.

11:39.760 --> 11:40.170
Yes...

11:40.170 --> 11:43.430
We're not making any progress here.

11:43.430 --> 11:44.560
Let Chieri talk.

11:44.560 --> 11:47.010
I-I want Chieri Onee-chan to do the talking, too.

11:47.010 --> 11:50.610
Well, that's um... you see... it's because...

11:50.610 --> 11:58.270
Yes, it's because I want you to experience the latest technology we just installed, the 3D virtual travel experience room.

11:58.940 --> 11:59.780
What is that?

11:59.780 --> 12:05.870
It's an amazing room that allows you to have an experience as if you are really there with just a push of a button.

12:05.870 --> 12:09.380
If you have something that interesting, hurry and take us there!

12:09.380 --> 12:11.080
I was about to fall asleep from boredom.

12:11.080 --> 12:13.950
Chief, that's not fully functional yet.

12:13.950 --> 12:16.820
Shh. I'm leaving you in charge
of cleaning up the mess afterwards.

12:16.820 --> 12:19.680
Let's move on, shall we?

12:23.120 --> 12:25.720
Something's not right with everyone.

12:47.660 --> 12:49.410
What is this place?

12:49.410 --> 12:50.660
It's pitch black.

12:52.080 --> 12:54.070
Please enjoy the show.

12:54.070 --> 12:56.500
How about we start off with Hawaii?

13:01.700 --> 13:03.130
Wow.

13:03.130 --> 13:06.840
How is it? But this isn't all.

13:10.420 --> 13:11.350
It's hot...

13:12.430 --> 13:14.120
But something's missing.

13:14.870 --> 13:17.520
No worries. The entire staff will work to find your standard.

13:18.580 --> 13:20.940
Ah right, the sound of waves!

13:22.150 --> 13:24.770
Please ignore the minor details.

13:25.270 --> 13:26.400
Welcome to Hawaii.

13:27.250 --> 13:30.990
Aloha.

13:35.940 --> 13:38.540
Let's check out more, shall we?

13:38.540 --> 13:39.880
On to Paris.

13:42.030 --> 13:43.540
It's cold!

13:46.560 --> 13:48.380
I've drawn your portrait.

13:48.820 --> 13:49.940
This isn't me!

13:49.940 --> 13:51.790
Calm down, please.

13:52.640 --> 13:53.770
I see.

13:53.770 --> 13:56.750
Mom, I want to go to Egypt.

13:57.550 --> 13:58.820
Leave it to me.

14:00.100 --> 14:01.610
Egypt.

14:01.610 --> 14:02.580
And the South Pole.

14:02.580 --> 14:03.610
America!

14:03.860 --> 14:04.860
India!

14:04.860 --> 14:05.730
Russia!

14:05.730 --> 14:07.250
Please stop.

14:07.250 --> 14:08.640
On bara bara.

14:08.110 --> 14:09.240
I'm not done playing yet.

14:09.240 --> 14:10.110
Mauritius.

14:10.110 --> 14:10.990
Holland.

14:10.990 --> 14:11.990
Mexico!

14:13.370 --> 14:15.000
It's going to break! It's going to break!

14:19.450 --> 14:20.440
Boring.

14:21.380 --> 14:22.710
Where's Mu?

14:22.710 --> 14:25.640
M-M-Mu?

14:25.640 --> 14:27.770
You're doing some interesting stuff.

14:28.220 --> 14:30.840
Let me join, Kitty.

14:30.840 --> 14:33.470
It doesn't come with Mu, so it's worthless.

14:33.470 --> 14:34.620
Forget about it.

14:34.620 --> 14:39.480
Now that we've played enough,
I'd like to hear what Chieri has to say.

14:38.820 --> 14:39.480
Gwashi!

14:40.100 --> 14:43.110
Well, Chieri-san hasn't been around for a while now.

14:43.110 --> 14:45.670
S-Sakurai went out for a bit for some personal business.

14:45.670 --> 14:47.990
Please, ladies, how about some juice?

14:48.400 --> 14:49.240
I've had enough.

14:51.480 --> 14:53.940
Lunch time. Let's go home, children.

14:53.940 --> 14:55.380
M-Midarezaki-sama?

14:55.740 --> 14:57.140
I'll come back after lunch.

14:57.140 --> 14:58.940
I expect to see Mu then.

15:03.190 --> 15:05.250
B-Branch Chief.

15:05.250 --> 15:08.780
You're an eyesore, Sakurai-kun.

15:08.780 --> 15:13.260
You work so efficiently and are trusted by the underlings.

15:13.260 --> 15:16.710
Are you after the seat of branch chief next?

15:16.710 --> 15:19.680
You're in my way for promotion.

15:20.340 --> 15:21.890
I don't have any intentions like that.

15:21.890 --> 15:24.020
I just want our customers to enjoy-

15:24.020 --> 15:25.640
Silence.

15:25.640 --> 15:28.780
There is no one who stands by your side.

15:28.780 --> 15:31.780
It's better for you to obey me.

15:32.500 --> 15:33.780
What do you mean?

15:34.580 --> 15:36.280
What did you do to Saitou-san and the others?

15:37.360 --> 15:39.850
I put them under a curse.

15:39.850 --> 15:43.170
Using the curse techniques I learned through a correspondence course.

15:43.760 --> 15:45.100
A curse?

15:45.100 --> 15:47.090
Much worse, correspondence course?

15:48.380 --> 15:53.010
I didn't want to resort to anything underhanded, but you leave me no choice.

15:53.010 --> 15:59.200
For the sake of my sales, I'll have the Midarezaki sign a contract no matter what.

16:00.190 --> 16:02.350
By any means.

16:03.230 --> 16:04.970
You can't curse the customers!

16:04.970 --> 16:05.800
Shut up!

16:05.800 --> 16:07.230
We don't have time!

16:07.230 --> 16:11.490
I will have you obey me even if it requires force.

16:12.750 --> 16:14.890
Branch Chief... Please stop...

16:16.000 --> 16:17.660
Branch... Chief...

16:20.790 --> 16:23.130
They weren't playing around with her.

16:23.130 --> 16:25.740
It looked more like they were being manipulated.

16:25.740 --> 16:29.140
Yeah, something was fishy with that dance.

16:29.140 --> 16:31.310
Plus, he had no fashion sense in picking the outfit.

16:31.310 --> 16:32.670
He looked like some spellcaster.

16:33.380 --> 16:35.610
Dances and spellcasters?

16:35.610 --> 16:37.690
I don't follow the story at all.

16:37.690 --> 16:40.200
I don't expect an amoeba to understand.

16:41.010 --> 16:43.310
By the way, what happened to the trip?

16:43.310 --> 16:44.660
Have you gotten tired of it already?

16:44.660 --> 16:47.170
Don't be a fool. The fun is only starting.

16:47.170 --> 16:51.820
You aren't giving the agency a headache by asking for the deep ocean or the Moon, are you?

16:53.130 --> 16:57.630
I want to go on a trip with Ouka and everyone else and have fun too.

16:57.630 --> 16:59.700
Yet, you don't believe me, do you, Ouka?

17:02.300 --> 17:08.370
So, Ouka, for the sake of a fun trip,
the second round will be full participation.

17:08.370 --> 17:10.670
Since it looks like there will be a use for you.

17:14.810 --> 17:17.300
We recommend this package...

17:18.550 --> 17:24.850
For the sake of the Branch Chief....

17:27.130 --> 17:29.190
The curse has been cast upon everyone.

17:29.190 --> 17:32.110
The entire staff is under my control.

17:33.210 --> 17:36.710
I didn't expect this to come in so handy.

17:36.710 --> 17:39.500
I'm glad I got a hold of this early on.

17:39.500 --> 17:42.650
I skipped the intermediate level, so I'm a little worried,

17:42.650 --> 17:45.120
but as expected from me. I'm managing to use it fine.

17:47.960 --> 17:49.250
Sorry to make you wait.

17:51.100 --> 17:53.630
You look more disgusting than before.

17:56.670 --> 17:58.590
I have powered up!

17:58.590 --> 18:01.140
I'm not the same as I was before!

18:01.710 --> 18:04.890
Kitty! You're so mean to go on ahead.

18:07.430 --> 18:08.800
I'm not done yet...

18:08.800 --> 18:10.900
Welcome aboard.

18:10.900 --> 18:11.650
Press.

18:12.690 --> 18:13.940
Chika!

18:21.720 --> 18:24.180
Welcome, Midarezaki-sama.

18:24.180 --> 18:29.500
After going through the power-up, we shall be the equal of anything you ask of us.

18:31.600 --> 18:33.090
Kitty, isn't this...

18:33.520 --> 18:38.130
When we do meet your standard,
I would like you to sign this agreement.

18:38.130 --> 18:41.260
Interesting. Then let me start tossing things out.

18:41.260 --> 18:42.430
Task one!

18:43.470 --> 18:44.760
Japan Trench!

18:55.780 --> 18:57.140
Hey, not bad.

18:57.140 --> 18:59.110
H-How is this the Japan Trench?

18:59.110 --> 19:00.030
Next!

19:00.990 --> 19:02.990
The Lighthouse of Alexandria!

19:02.990 --> 19:04.580
Oh yeah?

19:12.120 --> 19:14.000
N-Not bad.

19:14.750 --> 19:16.840
Those were nothing.

19:16.840 --> 19:18.270
I'm not done yet!

19:18.920 --> 19:20.510
The Bermuda Triangle!

19:20.510 --> 19:21.260
That's nothing!

19:28.850 --> 19:30.810
Have you made up your mind?

19:30.810 --> 19:34.150
Now, if you would sign this contract.

19:35.360 --> 19:38.180
Never! I don't accept it!

19:38.180 --> 19:38.940
Chika?

19:38.940 --> 19:42.950
I will never sign a contract for a trip without any love!

19:42.950 --> 19:47.580
A fun trip comes from all the laborious planning and preparations.

19:47.580 --> 19:50.330
All those are part of a fun trip!

19:51.290 --> 19:54.780
We can do anything about that once we have the contract.

19:54.780 --> 19:57.210
Playtime ends here!

19:59.330 --> 20:00.300
"Play?"

20:00.300 --> 20:01.900
That's my line.

20:01.900 --> 20:03.930
The party's only begun!

20:05.610 --> 20:06.680
What is this about?

20:08.770 --> 20:11.850
I won't forgive you if you hurt Mom and Nee-sama.

20:14.380 --> 20:15.950
Can I make a mess?

20:15.950 --> 20:17.860
Can I make a mess, Father?

20:17.860 --> 20:19.360
No, you can't be rough.

20:19.890 --> 20:22.320
You, too, Gekka. Don't shoot the beams so aimlessly.

20:22.320 --> 20:24.450
W-What is this?

20:25.690 --> 20:27.520
You don't know when to quit, do you?

20:27.520 --> 20:30.020
I'm from the Great Japanese Empire Paranormal Phenomena Bureau of Measures, 1st Counter Department,

20:30.020 --> 20:32.680
squad captain, Midarezaki Ouka.

20:33.380 --> 20:35.400
You're under arrest for the illegal usage of curses.

20:35.830 --> 20:38.540
The people in charge are on their way from the Bureau, too.

20:39.840 --> 20:42.700
Father, I found Chieri-san.

20:42.700 --> 20:44.720
But something looks strange.

20:45.230 --> 20:46.720
Ginka! She's still dangerous!

20:49.890 --> 20:54.350
Branch Chief... Please escape.

20:54.350 --> 20:57.920
No! Not my face! Stab my body if you must!

20:55.600 --> 20:59.900
Branch Chief... Please escape.

20:58.960 --> 20:59.900
Wait!

20:59.900 --> 21:01.670
You won't get away!

21:02.830 --> 21:05.150
You're so mean to throw me, Mother.

21:07.900 --> 21:08.670
What?

21:09.200 --> 21:10.960
What was I doing?

21:10.960 --> 21:13.200
Thank goodness, you're back with us.

21:13.570 --> 21:14.870
What am I doing?!

21:15.500 --> 21:16.820
What have I done...

21:17.220 --> 21:19.880
To attempt hurting our dear customer...

21:19.880 --> 21:23.290
I can't keep working in this job.

21:23.290 --> 21:24.340
I will quit as an apology.

21:25.380 --> 21:26.330
Nonsense.

21:26.330 --> 21:30.550
Bacteria swimming in the deep ocean would say something a thousand times better than what you just said.

21:30.550 --> 21:32.350
Or is that all you're capable of?

21:32.350 --> 21:35.980
But I don't have any other way of taking responsibility for the mess-up I've made.

21:35.980 --> 21:37.190
You idiot!

21:37.190 --> 21:39.900
What did you work so hard for to this day?

21:39.900 --> 21:43.110
Have you forgotten those who are longing to go on a vacation?

21:45.320 --> 21:48.990
Nee-sama, I'm simply looking forward to the honeymoon.

21:48.990 --> 21:51.740
I will thoroughly destroy your plan, too.

21:52.620 --> 21:54.000
I'm so tired.

21:54.000 --> 21:56.250
I want to go to somewhere soothing.

22:01.560 --> 22:03.210
I'm at your service.

22:03.210 --> 22:06.260
Always with a smile, and customers always come first!

22:06.260 --> 22:08.080
Yeah!

23:41.270 --> 23:42.270
This is Yuuka.

23:42.270 --> 23:43.350
It's the honeymoon.

23:43.350 --> 23:46.860
I'm simply happy to be able to go on a trip with everyone.

23:47.510 --> 23:50.950
Wait, but do honeymoons usually go like that?

23:51.310 --> 23:53.910
Next time: Survival Honeymoon.
